feat(update): warm-pull endpoint — pre-stage image before apply

Roadmap item 12 second half. Adds a "Prepare update" path so the slow
docker-pull happens while the old version is still serving traffic.
The eventual /apply then skips the pull (image already local) and
swap-restart is the only customer-visible downtime.

Updater side (updater/server.ts):
  POST /warm-pull { imageRepo, imageTag, sha256? }
  -> { ok, ref, digestVerified, elapsedMs }
  - Plain `docker pull` of the target ref. No volume snapshot, no
    compose touch, no version-pin write. Idempotent; safe to retry.
  - If sha256 supplied, verifies the local image's RepoDigest matches
    before reporting ok. Mismatch -> 409 (digest drift -> refuse).
  - Same handshake gate as /apply (PSK+HMAC+nonce).

Backend side (backend/src/routes/admin-update.ts):
  POST /api/admin/update/warm-pull
  - Admin-only, rate-limit 6/min/IP.
  - Looks up manifest, refuses if already up to date.
  - Signs request with updater PSK, forwards to unix socket.
  - 16-minute fetch timeout (large images on slow links).

Tradeoff: warm-pull leaves the new image on disk even if the admin
never clicks apply. `docker image prune` reclaims it. Acceptable —
disk is cheap, surprise downtime during pull is not.

Build verified, 61/61 lib tests pass.